codex
One distinction changes the split: a later read started by a fresh debugger `pc=` command can run even if the preceding store did not. I’m requiring either evidence specific to that store or a checkpoint reached through its guest continuation. That matters especially for the PCC2 unchanged-state rows and SGI survival checks.

codex
The value checks need the same scrutiny as the negative checks. For example, ASIC’s `sweep 256` assigns its “success” value through the debugger after the sweep; the returned value proves no guest access occurred. I also found unchanged-state checks whose readbacks run independently of the write they are meant to assess.

codex
To be precise: that ASIC value proves only that the debugger handled the assignment. It supplies no evidence that the guest sweep ran.

